WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:11.980
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.840
Tsukikage kooru daichi wo

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.670
Korogari fumiwakete yuku

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:40.880
Horobi to saisei no jidai ga hajimaru

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.550
Jiyuu wo omoku kakagete

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.120
Michinaki michi wo erande

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:55.230
Mahiru yori mabushii nichibotsu wo koete

00:00:55.230 --> 00:01:02.230
Yume wo kataru you ni toki no fune wa yuku

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:11.340
Sono yamiji no mukou ni atarashii yoake

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:19.250
Bokura wa kitto kurayami no kaina kara umarete kita

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.790
Kanawanu koi wo suruyou ni

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.760
Hikari e to samayotteku

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.000
Doko made mo hateshino nai kono michi wo

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.490
Kaeru sube wa nai

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:05.590
What?

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.720
Is that true?

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.870
Lord Shoten!

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.140
This must be about Yojiro.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.470
Yes.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.970
O Pitiable Eternal Assassin...

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:28.680
Because you don't know your own destiny,
you let destiny kill you.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.660
No!

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.330
Doctor.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.930
Ryoun Takamatsu

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.930
Give this to the patient we saw earlier.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:56.150
You must be hungry. I'll ask them
to make something for you right now.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:08.180
No!

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.420
Ezo Uchiura Bay Washinoki

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:15.690
That's Ezo!
That must be it!

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.370
Ezo!

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:18.630
We're here!

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.650
It is the 20th day of the tenth month,
in the first year of the Meiji era.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:28.750
The Enomoto Fleet, split in two groups,

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.080
Washinoki

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.080
Kakkumi

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.080
Tougeshita

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.080
Goryokaku

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.380
The Enomoto Fleet, split in two groups,

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:36.450
lands on Washinoki Beach and advances
towards Goryokaku in Hakodate.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:36.090
The Ujutai

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.620
Keisuke Otori

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:43.290
The Sajutai

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.690
Tetsunosuke Ichimura

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.640
Hakodate was originally under the direct
control of the Shogunate government

00:03:52.740 --> 00:04:00.950
Hakodate

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.470
and has flourished as a trading port
because of its rich fishing industry.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.810
Ships from Russia and Europe
made their way to Hakodate,

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:03.350
and many foreign nations established
embassies in Hakodate.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:07.780
What would happen if the flames of war
reached this town?

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:13.020
That was the reason why Enomoto avoided
landing directly on Hakodate.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:14.620
Goryokaku

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:14.620
Hakodate

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:21.830
Enomoto's army crushes Hakodate's forces,
which were a part of the New Government Army,

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.870
but by the time they
reach Hakodate,

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.710
Kinnaru Shimizudani

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:31.440
Hakodate's Governor Kinnaru Shimizudani
has already fled Goryokaku


00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.570
and crossed the sea to Aomori.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:46.920
Goryokaku is a castle modeled after the
castle cities of Europe during the middle ages.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:51.600
It took seven years to complete.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:53.570
Goryokaku

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.670
At the center of this pentagram-shaped fortress

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.900
Hakodate Magistrate Office

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:57.390
stands the Hakodate Magistrate Office.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.410
What is this?

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.640
It looks like someone's already been here.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.310
Could it be a thief?

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.990
There's nothing more miserable
than a castle without its master.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:19.420
Just like us...

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.330
Enomoto's army decides to use
Goryokaku as the base

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.670
from which to launch the counterattack
against the New Government Army.

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.770
As they swiftly reinforce the castle,

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:37.230
they begin planning to take over the only
other province in Ezo, Matsumae.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:44.970
Security is tighter now. It's difficult to infiltrate.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.050
Don't tell me you're going to just give up.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:53.360
No way! Then that would mean
we remained in Hakodate for nothing!

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:54.690
I know that.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:06:00.330
Governor Shimizudani was driven out of his
hometown and forced to escape across the sea.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.270
What would he think
if he heard this conversation?

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:09.070
Now is our chance. We, the Yuguntai, must
infiltrate their base and throw them into panic...

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:11.240
I know.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:16.340
We've got plans and the time will come for sure.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:22.510
Hakodate Hospital

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.820
Please place it there.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:30.620
Please take care of this one too.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.700
Tetsu, I'm sorry, but will you...

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:38.860
No!

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:54.250
Why would I have to take care of a woman?

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:57.680
Not only that, she's some random
traveling actor...

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:00.330
I'll have someone else do it if you don't want to.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.760
He can be my page as well.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.690
S-Sensei! Why, Sensei?

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:08.820
Why did you allow people
like her to travel with us?

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.700
Ask Enomoto.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:19.570
I'm asking you! Wasn't this our war?
The samurai's war?

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:24.180
This is a samurai's war.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.850
If you are samurai, follow orders
as a samurai should.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.420
Don't put too much thought into it, Tetsunosuke.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:36.920
<i>SHIN</i>

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:39.350
I'm coming in.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.970
Even though you're just a girl...

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.080
Eat everything you're given. If you don't...

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:03.120
What?

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:07.860
It's bad for your health!
That's what Ryoun-sensei was saying too!

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:08.990
Just eat!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:19.030
Hey, is that your sword?

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.280
W-wait just a second, everyone!

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.750
Doctor?

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.820
Please!

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:41.780
Please let me do my job as a doctor!
Let me treat you!

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:46.100
I've come as a member of Enomoto's army.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:49.860
I might be an enemy to those
who were here until yesterday,

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:53.230
but before that I'm a doctor!

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.440
There's neither friend nor foe
when it comes to patients!

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.140
I'll see anyone! I'll treat everyone!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.200
Please! I'm begging you!

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:10.860
Haven't any of you seen this woman
at your usual spots?

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.820
<i>KOTOHA</i>
<i>TAYU</i>

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:14.260
No...

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:15.730
Take a good look at her!

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:20.160
There's no way you'd forget a beauty like her!

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:22.860
Sorry, Mister.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:31.000
I've come this far north only because
I figured Tayu would be here...

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:34.710
Where did you go, Tayu?

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:48.020
I'm coming in.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:30.560
Do you intend to run from that katana, Leader?

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:41.740
Even if you get rid of it
your destiny will not disappear.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.180
But...

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:48.140
But my destiny was to go with
Akizuki-sama and...

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:52.620
No, that wasn't it...

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:57.690
I... I killed him... With my hands...
With this sword, Akizuki-sama...

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:08.430
That man... Yojiro Akizuki is alive.

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:13.000
What? What did you just say, Master?

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:19.170
Both of you must find out the truth of
your destiny while you're alive.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.920
The time will surely come.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.990
And I know that your katana
is aware of that as well.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:31.500
Kono tokoro tsuzuiteru nagaame ga
The rain that's been falling for so long

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:34.500
Akizuki-sama is alive... Akizuki-sama is alive!

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:37.470
Hayaru kimochi wo osae konde
Restrains my rushing feelings

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:49.450
Togireru koto no nai koukai ga maegami wo yurasu
Never-ending regret sways my bangs

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:40.410
He has to be alive...

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:43.040
...for my purpose as well.

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:50.720
Don't tell me she's going to!

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:55.390
Kurayami yori hito no yasashisa ni ashidome saresoude
It felt like kindness, rather than darkness

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.190
Don't do it!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:54.890
Hey, you!

00:11:55.390 --> 00:12:01.430
Kurayami yori hito no yasashisa ni ashidome saresoude
Was going to strand me

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:56.520
Don't die!

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:06.230
Anata tono yakusoku wo mabuta ni omoi kaeshiteta
I closed my eyes and thought about

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:03.930
What?

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:13.590
Anata tono yakusoku wo mabuta ni omoi kaeshiteta
The promise I repeatedly made with you

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:11.570
I-If you die my master would be...

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:16.570
What's so funny?

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:17.580
Namida
Tears

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:21.410
I'm sorry, but I'm not going to die.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:22.110
What?

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.310
What?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:27.690
Kuchikaketa tsuki ga ukanda
The decayed moon appears

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.490
I'm not going to kill myself. I'm not samurai.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.620
Namida
Tears

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.990
Do you mean to ridicule the samurai?

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:34.160
Namida ga tsutaeru subete wo
I don't want to miss any of the messages

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:41.430
Hitotsu mo nogasanai kimochi de
That the tears bring

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:37.330
Now I've made up my mind.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:39.600
H-hey, wait!

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:41.430
That's right.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:44.230
I'll stay alive and wait to
see where this destiny leads me...

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.300
With him...

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:50.070
Hakodate Port

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:53.810
This is brutal!

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.240
It's cold!

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.550
It's snow!

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.050
Here I go!

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:02.940
There!

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:07.620
I wonder if Master is really in a place like this...

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:09.480
Shiranui, too...

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.800
Oh, stop it, Gen!

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:20.460
I've got a message from a comrade.

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:24.740
Supposedly Enomoto and Hijikata
will leave Goryokaku this afternoon.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.240
Is that true?

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.650
So where are they going?

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:33.780
Hakodate Hospital.

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:38.920
They're going to check on their subordinates
who were injured in battle earlier.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:41.790
Security at the hospital shouldn't be too tight.

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:44.030
A chance like this doesn't come by too often.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:45.000
Let's do it!

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.400
Thank you!

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:54.840
Where did she go...

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:55.970
Long time no see!

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:01.070
Ta-Ta-Ta-Ta-Tayu?!

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:03.880
<i>Kakunojo</i>
<i>Yuyama</i>

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.360
Bathroom!

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.900
Again?

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:29.160
Oh?

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.940
Which way was it?

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.960
Master!

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:07.310
Thank you for coming so far.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:12.110
Actually we thought you'd
tricked us up until now.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.640
Have I ever tricked you before?

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:22.820
True... Thanks to you, we were able
to put an end to Nakaiya.

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:29.990
So, what kind of play are you writing this time?

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:32.130
Impressive insight as always, Zagashira.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:39.070
But I still don't have enough actors to raise
the banner of the Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe.

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:44.470
Actually, we've disbanded the troupe,
and the leader has been...

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:48.050
Your Leader is here in Hakodate.

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:49.880
Is that true?

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.210
She's here?

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:52.750
Where?

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.120
Where is she?

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:15.040
Hitotsu, higure ni gan kakete
One, make a wish on a sunset

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:24.380
Futatsu, fudasho no tsukimiso
Two, the primrose at the temple

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:30.900
Mittsu, misora ga akeru koro
Three, around the time when the
beautiful sky opens up

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:35.090
Oh boy... She puts a doctor to shame.
Mittsu, misora ga akeru koro
Three, around the time when the
beautiful sky opens up

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.330
Don't move! Or I'll kill you!

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:41.940
Who are you?

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:43.030
This is a hospital!

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:49.280
Shit!

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:53.780
Calm down, Doctor.
We're members of the Yuguntai.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.320
Yuguntai?

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:58.290
We have no intention to harm you guys.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:16:59.680
They're not here yet!

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:03.230
But I'm going to perform a surgery today.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:05.000
Do it some other time.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.120
That's nonsense! The life of this patient
depends on the surgery!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:19.010
Doctor!

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:22.310
Hijikata's visit has been cancelled.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:23.510
What?

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:25.440
What's going on?

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.680
Stop joking around, you little brat!

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:29.920
Who are you people?

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:33.860
I get it. You must've come here to ambush them!

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:37.280
Are you assassins?

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.830
Stop making noise, Kid!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.360
Just be quiet!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:45.740
Stop it!

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:50.170
Now you have no business here!
Just get out of here now!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:51.400
Shut up!

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:54.640
What the hell's going on?

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:57.440
Something must've happened.

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:59.810
What? Something happened?

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:06.390
Is that true that the messenger
we sent to Fukuyama has been killed?

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:13.700
He was taken prisoner,
then executed as a traitor.

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:19.830
I told you this wouldn't work!
Asking them to surrender was pointless!

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:22.630
What are you going to do now, Enomoto?

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:32.280
Now we have an excuse
to destroy Matsumae Province.

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:36.250
We can control all of Ezo!

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:42.250
Send the Kaiten and Banryu out!

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:46.720
Hijikata's squad is going to attack
Fukuyama Castle by land!

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:53.360
I'm not going to believe
what a little brat like him told us!

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:54.540
Stop it!

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:55.600
Die, you bastard!

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:03.950
Wh-who are you?

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:06.270
Women and kids should stay out of this!

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:13.080
A samurai who swings his sword around
at a hospital is lower than women and children.

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:15.750
Even I know that much.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.660
You get out of here now!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.590
Don't you mess with me, woman!

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:27.940
What?

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:29.630
Damn you!

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:36.010
It's been a while.

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:38.910
I'm jealous that you got
the spotlight all to yourself!

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:40.940
Long time no see!

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:44.850
I'm jealous that only you two
get to play the parts!

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:47.150
We're jealous, too!

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:48.820
Everyone...

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:51.460
Guys...

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:59.790
Leave!
Get out of here now!

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:04.610
Everyone...

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:07.510
How dare you!

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:10.040
That's enough! Let's get out of here!

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.350
You two...

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:19.790
Everyone!

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:20.650
Yeah!

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:29.800
This is our first time in Hakodate!

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:35.500
We're the Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe!

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:40.900
Oh... Amazing!

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:44.080
Kakunojo Yuyama...

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:45.780
Leader, you seem to be doing well.

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:47.750
What are you doing here?

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.450
Leader!

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:51.320
Zagashira!

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:59.250
I see, you guys must be in Ibaragi's play...
This is great!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:05.770
Doctors and hospitals aren't
the only ways to treat patients.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:10.040
Ibaragi must've thought about it, then...
I'm impressed!

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.110
Shogunate Remnants Fleet:           Kaiten Banryu

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.350
It is the eleventh month of the
first year of the Meiji Era.

00:21:21.350 --> 00:21:28.990
The all-out battle of the men who stake their
destinies in the northern lands is about to begin.

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:37.160
Mutsunokuni

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:40.400
